==============================================================================
Third-party components
==============================================================================

1) llama.cpp — https://github.com/ggml-org/llama.cpp
   The on-device inference engine used by the NETMIND Android node.
   Pinned release: v1.1.0. License: MIT.
   The source is fetched at build time by scripts/fetch-llama.sh and is not
   vendored in this repository.

2) Arm AI Chat Android binding (examples/llama.android in llama.cpp)
   JNI binding, Kotlin inference-engine facade and build configuration that
   the NETMIND `android/lib` module is derived from. License: MIT (as part of
   the llama.cpp repository).

3) Model weights offered by the in-app downloader:
   - Qwen3-0.6B (Apache-2.0) — https://huggingface.co/Qwen/Qwen3-0.6B
   - Qwen2.5-0.5B-Instruct (Apache-2.0) — https://huggingface.co/Qwen/Qwen2.5-0.5B-Instruct
   Model files are downloaded by the end user at runtime and are never
   redistributed through this repository.

These open-weight models are stored and executed exclusively on the user's
own device. NETMIND contains no integration with any vendor inference API.
